Verification
Checklist
Verify your installation and configuration:

Service Status:
sudo systemctl is-active postgresql
# Expected: active
User Roles Exist:
sudo -u postgres psql -c "\du"
# Should list: db_admin, app_user, readonly_user
Database Exists:
sudo -u postgres psql -c "\l" | grep testdb
# Should show testdb owned by app_user
Authentication Works:
psql -U app_user -d testdb -h localhost -c "SELECT current_user;"
# Should return: app_user
Permissions Correct:
# Test write permission
psql -U app_user -d testdb -h localhost -c "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM products;"

# Test read-only restriction
psql -U readonly_user -d testdb -h localhost -c "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM products;"
Troubleshooting Tips
Issue: Cannot connect to PostgreSQL

Check service status: sudo systemctl status postgresql
Verify port is listening: sudo ss -tunelp | grep 5432
Check pg_hba.conf authentication rules
Issue: Password authentication fails

Verify user exists: sudo -u postgres psql -c "\du"
Check pg_hba.conf has md5 method for the connection type
Ensure you restarted PostgreSQL after config changes
Issue: Permission denied errors

Verify role privileges: \du in psql
Check database ownership: \l in psql
Grant necessary permissions using GRANT statements
Issue: Cannot find configuration files

Ubuntu/Debian: /etc/postgresql/[version]/main/
CentOS/RHEL: /var/lib/pgsql/data/
Use: sudo -u postgres psql -c "SHOW config_file;"
