Key Takeaways:

PostgreSQL uses role-based authentication and authorization
The pg_hba.conf file controls client authentication methods
Different authentication methods (md5, scram-sha-256, peer) serve different security needs
Proper user role configuration is essential for database security
Always restart PostgreSQL after configuration changes
